WEBVTT

00:08.150 --> 00:08.200
Miyakogawa Landscaping

00:59.500 --> 00:59.750
The true forms

01:01.330 --> 01:01.580
Of the things that I gazed at

01:03.210 --> 01:03.460
Were for showing after I closed my eyes

01:04.290 --> 01:07.170
Shigofumi

01:06.920 --> 01:07.170
Again today, time

01:08.760 --> 01:09.010
Will only construct a loneliness

01:10.550 --> 01:10.800
That seems to be torn apart, right?

01:17.970 --> 01:18.220
There are people who can't forget about

01:21.640 --> 01:21.890
The white lotuses that bloom in the darkness

01:25.270 --> 01:25.520
Nevertheless, recollections

01:29.030 --> 01:29.280
Visit from the future

01:32.700 --> 01:32.950
Words that turn into sighs

01:40.120 --> 01:40.370
Are the emerging wings of the soul

01:43.790 --> 01:44.040
Will I flutter apart?

01:47.500 --> 01:47.750
Growing confused and disordered

01:51.170 --> 01:51.420
I want to carve

01:53.510 --> 01:53.760
These letters to you

01:58.510 --> 01:58.770
Pieces of the truth

02:00.350 --> 02:00.600
Of things that I want to tell you-

02:02.230 --> 02:02.480
I can't even send them well to you

02:05.980 --> 02:06.230
If I write them with the blood that stains my fingertips

02:09.650 --> 02:09.900
Then can they spill into your heart?

02:13.320 --> 02:13.570
Even if the one word left behind

02:16.570 --> 02:16.820
To us who live

02:19.240 --> 02:19.490
Is to be goodbye

02:28.750 --> 02:30.250
I heard there were cases overseas...

02:30.710 --> 02:34.130
where people have woken up from
listening to people talking to them.

02:34.130 --> 02:35.680
Even though they're in a coma?

02:35.680 --> 02:39.310
I guess it's probably because it
reached their innermost consciousness.

02:39.310 --> 02:41.850
Even if their brains can't process the language.

02:41.850 --> 02:45.020
Note: The word for innermost consciousness sounds similar to the Japanese word for the part of brain which specializes in language.

02:41.850 --> 02:43.140
Diving beetle?

02:45.310 --> 02:46.350
Fumi-chan.

02:47.860 --> 02:51.320
We went to Mikawa Kirameki's place.

02:51.980 --> 02:54.070
He hasn't changed at all.

02:54.610 --> 02:57.160
He'd completely lost his ability to write though.

02:57.870 --> 03:00.660
But, he has a good manager now.

03:03.200 --> 03:04.790
It's Natsuka's sister.

03:05.870 --> 03:08.840
You still remember Natsuka and Kaname, don't you?

03:09.380 --> 03:12.380
They've come to visit you.

03:13.130 --> 03:16.510
Fumi-chan, let's go to school once again.

03:16.510 --> 03:20.970
We've not participated in culture
festivals, athletic meets or clubs yet.

03:21.970 --> 03:24.480
And make plenty of friends too.

03:25.270 --> 03:26.940
I'll be waiting for you too.

03:26.940 --> 03:29.810
Say, it's been on my mind for a while, but...

03:29.810 --> 03:33.320
wasn't it Mika I talked to when we first met at the infirmary?

03:34.570 --> 03:35.950
Really?

03:35.950 --> 03:38.360
No, I've...

03:38.360 --> 03:39.740
never been to school...

03:40.320 --> 03:45.540
When I first talked to her, Fumika seemed to stiffen up, but...

03:51.880 --> 03:55.970
Note: Fumika uses "boku" to refer to herself here. It is usually used by males when referring to themselves.

03:51.880 --> 03:55.970
I'm Mikawa Fumika. Nice to meet you.

03:56.880 --> 03:58.590
After all, she used, "boku".

03:59.300 --> 04:02.600
So, you've been to school too, Fumika.

04:02.600 --> 04:04.890
School does sound fun, eh?

04:04.890 --> 04:07.390
I was hoping to break the ice for her.

04:07.390 --> 04:10.230
So that Fumi-chan could make friends.

04:10.810 --> 04:14.940
<i>So, the one I had a crush on... Could it be...?</i>

04:15.230 --> 04:18.280
Fumika, don't we have to go soon?

04:18.280 --> 04:19.200
Yeah.

04:19.200 --> 04:21.280
This just doesn't feel right.

04:21.280 --> 04:25.160
How unusual of the business-minded Fumika-san.

04:25.700 --> 04:29.170
This one may be a bit difficult.

04:29.170 --> 04:31.830
Can you please explain to me, Fumika...

04:31.830 --> 04:33.590
What's a Shigofumi?

04:33.590 --> 04:37.170
I understand that it's a letter from a dead person, but...

04:41.720 --> 04:46.810
Not confined to just letters, anything can be
delivered as long as you stick a Shigofumi stamp on it.

04:47.100 --> 04:50.940
So, is that Fumika's real body
that everyone has been talking about?

04:51.060 --> 04:52.440
She looks just like you.

04:52.440 --> 04:55.230
I thought it was strange that you aged.

04:55.230 --> 04:57.690
But, it's because you aren't dead.

04:58.740 --> 05:01.240
Matoma, you said that you wouldn't tell anyone.

05:01.240 --> 05:02.740
I typed it out.

05:03.660 --> 05:07.830
It's okay. I've not told the other postal workers.

05:08.410 --> 05:10.000
Did you come to see me on purpose?

05:10.000 --> 05:11.580
Of course not.

05:11.580 --> 05:14.130
I'm not that free.

05:14.130 --> 05:15.290
Then, why?

05:15.800 --> 05:17.090
Want to go have some fun?

05:17.090 --> 05:18.880
I still have some catnip left.

05:18.880 --> 05:20.510
So, you really are free.

05:20.510 --> 05:22.800
I'm always looking at mountains.

05:22.800 --> 05:26.760
So, let's go to the sea; like the southern islands or
something. It's part of forming relationships too.

05:26.760 --> 05:29.480
You guys come too. It's summer vacation already, isn't it?

05:29.480 --> 05:30.640
Can we?

05:30.640 --> 05:35.230
You may be free, but we've got work to do after this.

05:35.230 --> 05:36.150
So...

05:36.150 --> 05:37.150
Very well.

05:38.030 --> 05:39.110
Is it okay?

05:39.110 --> 05:40.610
You understand that feeling too?

05:40.610 --> 05:44.570
But in exchange, I'd like to choose the destination.

05:49.160 --> 05:51.960
I never expected you to really choose the southern islands.

05:51.960 --> 05:53.670
Though it's still inside the country.

05:53.670 --> 05:55.130
Why didn't we just fly there?

05:55.130 --> 06:00.300
Part of the fun of travelling is how you get there.

06:00.300 --> 06:01.760
I fail to understand humans.

06:01.760 --> 06:03.470
I understand though.

06:03.470 --> 06:05.090
Movement is fun, right?

06:05.720 --> 06:07.560
Movement?

06:07.850 --> 06:09.350
I think you got it wrong.

06:09.350 --> 06:12.850
No, I didn't. Because I'm going to become human.

06:12.850 --> 06:14.940
All this dreamy talk again.

06:14.940 --> 06:16.900
My dreams are dreams that will come true!

06:16.900 --> 06:20.400
Chiaki-san, you're a postal worker too, aren't you?

06:20.400 --> 06:22.990
That's right. I'm Fumika's senior.

06:22.990 --> 06:24.700
Then, um...

06:25.740 --> 06:26.780
Yes, I'm dead.

06:28.120 --> 06:29.950
It was in a car accident.

06:29.950 --> 06:33.620
It was <i>boom</i>! A head-on collision with an oncoming vehicle.

06:34.460 --> 06:36.420
It was a short life.

06:36.420 --> 06:38.670
So, you were a terrible driver?

06:38.670 --> 06:43.720
Don't be stupid. Driving is something you make guys do for you.

06:44.720 --> 06:48.680
Well, if there's anything you'd like to know
about boy-girl matters, feel free to ask big sister.

06:48.680 --> 06:49.810
Master!

06:52.310 --> 06:53.560
You too, young man.

06:54.350 --> 06:56.060
Why me?

06:56.060 --> 06:59.570
You were screaming, "Fumika,
I love you!", while facing the sunset, weren't you?

07:02.230 --> 07:04.030
What kind of stories have you been telling?

07:04.030 --> 07:05.610
It's the truth though, isn't it?

07:05.610 --> 07:07.410
Fumika, I love you!

07:07.410 --> 07:08.240
Cut it out!

07:08.240 --> 07:12.040
Fumika! Fumika, I love you!

07:09.490 --> 07:10.870
I told you to stop.

07:10.870 --> 07:12.040
That's nice.

07:12.040 --> 07:13.660
Will you cut it out!?

07:27.760 --> 07:29.930
Is this our room?

07:38.060 --> 07:41.610
Don't tell me this is the first time
you're staying in a traveller's lodge?

07:41.610 --> 07:44.030
This is the first time I've been on a vacation.

07:44.030 --> 07:46.070
Huh? The actual vacation itself?

07:46.070 --> 07:47.030
Yes.

07:47.030 --> 07:52.330
All right! Then allow us to teach
you how to have fun during vacations.

07:52.330 --> 07:53.120
First!

07:54.330 --> 07:55.250
What are you doing?

07:55.250 --> 07:57.540
It's called a pillow-fight. Take this!

07:57.540 --> 07:59.380
Me too! Let me play too!

08:07.470 --> 08:10.300
Should I serve some tea?

08:10.300 --> 08:11.550
I don't mind.

08:13.470 --> 08:14.930
Suitenguu Island?

08:15.640 --> 08:16.600
Yes.

08:17.440 --> 08:20.860
It's uninhabited and there's nothing there now, though.

08:20.860 --> 08:22.360
I'm aware.

08:23.230 --> 08:24.690
But, I'd like to go there.

08:27.150 --> 08:29.110
Full Name

08:27.150 --> 08:29.110
Address

08:27.150 --> 08:29.110
Nojima

08:27.150 --> 08:29.110
Kaname

08:27.900 --> 08:29.110
The next island?

08:29.110 --> 08:30.280
Yeah.

08:30.280 --> 08:34.330
Fumika says that our final
destination isn't here, but the next island.

08:34.330 --> 08:35.330
The next?

08:37.330 --> 08:39.620
I wonder what Fumika is thinking.

08:39.620 --> 08:40.920
You too, Kaname-kun.

08:40.920 --> 08:41.830
About what?

08:41.830 --> 08:44.460
You finally managed to see Fumika again and all.

08:44.460 --> 08:45.800
Aren't you going to confess?

08:45.800 --> 08:46.300
Huh?

08:46.300 --> 08:48.260
Fumika said it herself, didn't she?

08:48.590 --> 08:52.890
She was just startled back then,
and it wasn't that she disliked you.

08:53.300 --> 08:56.060
She's available, so try again.

08:56.060 --> 08:58.520
This was back in middle school, right?

08:58.520 --> 08:59.770
It's in the past.

08:59.770 --> 09:01.900
There's no such thing as "in the past" when it comes to love!

09:02.190 --> 09:03.690
You still like her, don't you?

09:03.690 --> 09:05.570
It's none of your business now, is it, Natsuka?

09:05.570 --> 09:06.530
It is.

09:06.530 --> 09:07.570
Why?

09:08.360 --> 09:12.700
Because... Fumika is my friend, and...

09:12.700 --> 09:14.700
This is what you call youth, isn't it?

09:14.700 --> 09:15.870
You have bad tastes.

09:15.870 --> 09:18.330
Using the communicator to snoop on them.

09:18.330 --> 09:21.290
What are you saying? This is a matter concerning you.

09:21.290 --> 09:22.250
Me?

09:22.250 --> 09:25.250
Didn't that glasses boy confess to you?

09:26.460 --> 09:30.930
What about you? Or is there someone else that you like?

09:30.930 --> 09:31.630
Yes.

09:31.630 --> 09:33.640
Eh? Really?

09:33.640 --> 09:36.350
Who? Someone alive? Someone dead?

09:37.310 --> 09:38.350
Fumi-chan.

09:38.930 --> 09:41.940
That's you, isn't it?! And a girl too!

09:43.150 --> 09:45.940
Love - I don't really understand what it means.

09:46.820 --> 09:51.780
That's right. You were always alone with your father.

09:52.450 --> 09:53.360
Yeah.

09:53.360 --> 09:54.370
What about you, Chiaki?

09:54.370 --> 09:55.160
Me?

09:55.160 --> 09:58.870
Have you done it a lot? Love and romance.

09:58.870 --> 10:00.370
You could say that.

10:01.460 --> 10:02.580
But...

10:04.830 --> 10:06.500
It was a long time ago...

10:11.630 --> 10:13.090
This is?

10:13.090 --> 10:16.680
Yes, that's Mikawa Kirameki-sensei's manuscript.

10:16.680 --> 10:19.310
Really? You did well in getting it.

10:19.310 --> 10:20.770
Thank you very much.

10:22.810 --> 10:26.150
Excuse me, I've made a reservation here. I'm Shirakawa.

10:34.570 --> 10:35.570
Say...

10:36.570 --> 10:38.280
Why did you come with us?

10:39.080 --> 10:42.410
To this southern island. You had work to do, didn't you?

10:42.910 --> 10:44.790
I'm working right now.

10:44.790 --> 10:46.920
Huh? But...

10:46.920 --> 10:52.050
Ah, I know. There's a Shigofumi to
be delivered on that island, right?

10:58.640 --> 10:59.930
Excuse me.

11:00.220 --> 11:03.930
But, the old lady we asked earlier
said that it was an uninhabited island.

11:04.230 --> 11:07.940
Come on, Fumika. Who's on that island?

11:08.690 --> 11:09.400
A dead person.

11:10.610 --> 11:12.280
Are you talking about a postal worker?

11:12.280 --> 11:14.280
No, it might be just a corpse.

11:14.280 --> 11:15.860
An abandoned corpse?

11:15.860 --> 11:18.870
Please cut it out. We're going to that island soon and all.

11:19.580 --> 11:21.370
Dead people are quiet.

11:21.790 --> 11:23.160
Are you serious?

11:23.160 --> 11:27.000
It'll be okay. The living are far scarier after all.

11:27.000 --> 11:29.290
What if the murderer is there?

11:29.290 --> 11:30.670
Oh, you have a point there.

11:30.670 --> 11:33.300
Might be a recent murder too.

11:33.300 --> 11:35.840
He might be burying the murder weapon as we speak.

11:36.090 --> 11:38.300
Don't say that so nonchalantly.

11:38.300 --> 11:40.850
Come on, Fumika. No more of these sick jokes...

11:41.720 --> 11:42.640
Natsuka!

11:45.850 --> 11:47.190
M-Miss?

11:48.940 --> 11:50.860
Natsuka, are you all right?

11:51.190 --> 11:52.480
I'm fine.

11:52.480 --> 11:54.990
I'm sorry. Are you all right?

12:00.280 --> 12:02.740
Murder... weapon?

12:05.120 --> 12:07.120
Shigofumi

12:08.210 --> 12:10.210
Shigofumi

12:12.920 --> 12:15.630
Sorry for causing a scene.

12:16.510 --> 12:18.090
I'm visiting a grave.

12:18.590 --> 12:21.220
That sickle is for trimming the grass.

12:22.050 --> 12:23.350
Grave visit?

12:23.350 --> 12:25.640
That's admirable for someone so young.

12:25.640 --> 12:28.480
Yeah, I haven't made a visit myself in five years.

12:30.810 --> 12:33.570
Um, that's not all.

12:34.650 --> 12:37.190
Actually, there's someone I'm interested in.

12:37.700 --> 12:42.240
I'd like to confess to him, but
I just can't seem to gather the courage.

12:42.240 --> 12:43.370
Or, maybe I'm just scared.

12:44.740 --> 12:50.540
Right at that time, the love horoscope on TV
said that my "Love Lucky Chance" was a grave visit.

12:50.540 --> 12:51.920
And then?

12:53.340 --> 12:56.170
I see. You're part of the unrequited love group too, huh?

12:57.340 --> 12:59.800
Other than myself, everyone here currently has unrequited love.

12:59.800 --> 13:01.300
Really?

13:01.800 --> 13:02.850
Kinda...

13:03.510 --> 13:06.430
Is that how my relationship with Fumi-chan is seen?

13:06.430 --> 13:10.980
It's tough, isn't it? Confessions feel
like life-and-death situations, don't they?

13:10.980 --> 13:13.610
Once you step out, your life is on the line.

13:13.610 --> 13:14.480
I know!

13:14.480 --> 13:15.860
You do?

13:15.860 --> 13:21.110
Love might come true, but if you fail,
you can no longer return to even being friends.

13:21.110 --> 13:22.700
Youth is so great.

13:22.700 --> 13:25.660
Haven't you done something like that before, Chiaki-san?

13:25.660 --> 13:29.200
Well, I'm the one being confessed to.

13:30.040 --> 13:31.170
Really?

13:31.170 --> 13:34.080
There was this guy who was clueless about confessions.

13:34.630 --> 13:37.380
"Chiaki-san, I want to be your Mr Lightning Dodger."

13:38.800 --> 13:40.300
What does that mean?

13:40.300 --> 13:43.140
I'm sure he was trying to say lightning rod.

13:43.430 --> 13:45.890
Normally, it's supposed to be "shield", right?

13:46.180 --> 13:47.890
That's pretty poor taste as well.

13:49.350 --> 13:51.890
Chiaki-san, what are your pouring?

13:51.890 --> 13:53.690
I'm not a minor.

13:53.690 --> 13:55.360
We are minors though.

13:55.360 --> 13:59.780
Come on now, we can't talk about love when we're sober, right?

13:59.780 --> 14:02.320
You have a crush on that glasses boy, don't you?

14:02.820 --> 14:04.160
Is that so?

14:04.990 --> 14:07.740
Why are you sleeping, Fumika?

14:07.740 --> 14:08.830
You reek of alcohol.

14:08.830 --> 14:11.160
Telling people about your loves...

14:11.160 --> 14:12.870
is one of the great joys of travel.

14:13.170 --> 14:14.290
Get up!

14:15.330 --> 14:19.300
Okay, let's share your love
experiences going clockwise. First, Natsuka!

14:19.300 --> 14:21.090
Should I switch off the lights?

14:21.090 --> 14:21.880
Yeah.

14:25.890 --> 14:27.890
So sleepy...

14:27.890 --> 14:30.100
Because you were causing a ruckus all night.

14:30.100 --> 14:32.770
Girls' nights together are precious, you know?

14:33.060 --> 14:35.480
I learned lots.

14:37.020 --> 14:39.820
Are you going to visit the grave
the moment we reach the island?

14:39.820 --> 14:42.030
Would you like to swim with us?

14:42.030 --> 14:44.280
After the grave visit then.

14:44.280 --> 14:45.700
Okay, we'll be waiting.

14:45.700 --> 14:48.780
Which reminds me, whose grave are you visiting?

14:48.780 --> 14:50.410
My grandfather's.

14:50.410 --> 14:54.040
The Kiyosumi house used to be on that island.

14:55.460 --> 14:56.380
Kiyosumi?

14:56.380 --> 14:59.090
That's my grandfather's surname.

14:59.090 --> 15:02.920
I'm his daughter's daughter, so my surname is different.

15:02.920 --> 15:04.340
Ah, so that's why.

15:05.220 --> 15:07.640
What's your grandfather's name?

15:08.050 --> 15:09.470
Kiyosumi Saizo.

15:10.720 --> 15:13.810
That's cool! Was your grandfather a samurai?

15:13.810 --> 15:14.980
How could he be?

15:23.860 --> 15:25.200
I see.

15:27.110 --> 15:29.580
He married.

15:33.250 --> 15:34.960
It's a private beach!

15:34.960 --> 15:36.710
The sea feels so good!

15:38.960 --> 15:43.340
I wonder why Fumika chose this island.

15:43.340 --> 15:44.760
Come to think of it...

15:47.260 --> 15:52.100
But then again, swimming together with staves
is only possible on an uninhabited island, huh?

15:52.100 --> 15:53.180
Sure is.

15:53.180 --> 15:55.430
All right! Here I come!

15:56.140 --> 15:57.390
Not going to swim?

15:57.390 --> 15:58.810
What about yourself?

16:11.120 --> 16:12.160
Let's get started then.

16:12.620 --> 16:14.040
That time...

16:15.330 --> 16:18.170
I went to see the city where I was born...

16:18.170 --> 16:19.580
after all this time.

16:22.210 --> 16:25.130
But, there was nothing there.

16:25.630 --> 16:28.130
My house, my school...

16:28.130 --> 16:32.760
my favourite shops, even the park I often played at, everything.

16:33.430 --> 16:36.640
Fifty years have passed since I died.

16:36.640 --> 16:39.020
I guess it's only natural that things have changed.

16:39.480 --> 16:41.900
I'm the only one who hasn't changed.

16:41.900 --> 16:44.980
My parents and my friends have all passed away.

16:46.190 --> 16:47.900
Your lover too?

16:47.900 --> 16:49.240
Looks like it.

16:50.990 --> 16:53.080
Even though he survived the crash.

16:54.240 --> 16:58.410
But, he lived for fifty years after that, so it's all good.

16:58.910 --> 17:01.580
The cat person you were talking about before...

17:02.330 --> 17:05.250
I'm a little jealous that you can age.

17:08.220 --> 17:10.550
Chiaki, let's go.

17:10.550 --> 17:11.720
Huh?

17:11.720 --> 17:12.590
Where to?

17:13.430 --> 17:14.560
To that grave.

17:18.060 --> 17:19.980
Hey! That's not food.

17:25.190 --> 17:27.530
Can we join you?

17:29.530 --> 17:33.660
Grandpa, this is Fumika-san and Chiaki-san.

17:33.660 --> 17:36.240
We became friends on the way here.

17:43.830 --> 17:46.800
So, you died for real.

17:51.680 --> 17:53.680
Kiyosumi Saizo-kun...

17:54.600 --> 17:57.350
Did you live a happy life?

17:59.060 --> 18:00.180
I'm sure you did.

18:00.680 --> 18:06.230
Getting married and even having such
a lovely granddaughter - I'm sure you were happy.

18:07.440 --> 18:09.780
<i>You were my last love.</i>

18:09.780 --> 18:13.740
<i>But, you had your own life to live after that, right?</i>

18:15.570 --> 18:17.160
Okay, I'm done.

18:17.160 --> 18:18.410
You too, Fumika...

18:24.290 --> 18:26.630
That's my name...

18:27.000 --> 18:29.840
The sender is Kiyosumi Saizo.

18:29.840 --> 18:32.090
Then, your assignment was...

18:35.760 --> 18:38.180
Who could this person be?

18:38.180 --> 18:40.560
Grandpa had always been single.

18:40.560 --> 18:42.060
Eh, but...

18:42.060 --> 18:44.020
My mother was adopted.

18:44.020 --> 18:47.520
She lost her parents in a car
accident when she was still a toddler.

18:47.520 --> 18:49.610
And grandpa took her in.

20:04.020 --> 20:05.230
Say, Chiaki-san?

20:05.230 --> 20:06.180
What is it?

20:06.180 --> 20:07.520
Did you have fun today?

20:07.520 --> 20:08.190
Yeah.

20:08.480 --> 20:10.730
Was last week's movie fun too?

20:10.730 --> 20:11.650
Yeah.

20:12.520 --> 20:14.690
Was the art gallery fun too?

20:14.690 --> 20:15.490
Yeah.

20:15.780 --> 20:18.700
Everything has been fun since I met you.

20:18.700 --> 20:19.780
So...

20:24.290 --> 20:28.210
So, will you be with me forever from now on?

20:37.050 --> 20:40.640
You really are a fool.

20:41.890 --> 20:46.600
You should have just forgotten
about me, and searched for another girl.

20:47.180 --> 20:50.440
Also, don't you use a ring to propose?

20:50.440 --> 20:52.190
That's a gravestone.

20:53.110 --> 20:55.320
You are clueless as always.

20:59.990 --> 21:00.700
But...

21:14.340 --> 21:16.340
Yes, I do.

21:23.550 --> 21:26.770
Ahh, that feels so good.

21:26.770 --> 21:27.970
Do me next too!

21:28.980 --> 21:30.140
Natsuka-chan...

21:30.600 --> 21:33.190
I'm going to confess when I get back.

21:33.480 --> 21:34.900
You found the determination?

21:35.570 --> 21:38.110
Yeah, somehow.

21:51.250 --> 21:56.090
Shigofumi

21:51.250 --> 21:56.090
Episode Nine

21:51.250 --> 21:56.090
Reunion

23:26.890 --> 23:28.550
The man who dwells on the past.

23:28.890 --> 23:30.760
The girl who seeks the future.

23:31.560 --> 23:34.770
What connected them was a world created in fiction.

23:36.270 --> 23:37.900
Next time on Shigofumi:

23:38.440 --> 23:39.230
Encounter.

23:39.230 --> 23:41.230
Shigofumi

23:39.230 --> 23:41.230
Episode Ten
